# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Datasets — never committed. Re-create with:  python data_download.py
# (see docs/DATASETS.md for the two datasets that need a manual download)
#
# Everything under data/ is ignored EXCEPT the per-dataset README.md files,
# which are the documentation for data we don't store in git.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/**
!data/**/
!data/**/README.md

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Work in progress.
#
# A dataset folder sitting at the repo ROOT (instead of under data/) means it is
# the one being actively worked on -- see "Work in progress" in README.md.
# Same rule as data/: ignore the bulk, keep the README.md and the notebook.
#
# When a dataset moves back into data/ its line here becomes a no-op and can go.
# When you start on the next one, copy the three lines and change the name.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
chemical-process-monitoring-time-series-dataset/**
!chemical-process-monitoring-time-series-dataset/README.md
!chemical-process-monitoring-time-series-dataset/*.ipynb
!chemical-process-monitoring-time-series-dataset/*.py
!chemical-process-monitoring-time-series-dataset/identified_model.json

# Third-party reference catalogue, cloned not authored.
# Source: github.com/dalmia/awesome-industrial-datasets
awesome-industrial-datasets-master/

# Course lab submission bundles — the extracted work is already in archive/
archive/**/*.zip

# ─── Data file types, wherever they land ───
*.csv
*.tsv
*.parquet
*.wav
*.txt
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.bdf
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.npy
*.npz
# ...but keep dependency and doc text files
!requirements*.txt
!LICENSE*.txt

# ─── Python ───
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.env
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ─── Editors / OS ───
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
